From d498123cf0e558f3d4b0a909f37bdcd534de74d7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Tue, 19 May 2026 17:08:56 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] dos: Phase 11 patch 0067 (v2) -- SDL_DOSAudioPump bool return
 + iter cap

flush-instr's Leg A v1 iter verdict (486-CLASS-CAMPAIGN-FINDINGS.md
sec.17): Leg A failed freeze elimination + caused TAS desync. Root
cause -- per-pump bandwidth too low: ONE iterate per call = ~23 ms
audio = 138 ms coverage over 400-1400 ms load_stage windows = ~10%
coverage. The ring underruns mid-load even with six seam-pumps.

v2 fix specced by flush-instr: nxengine-evo/0162's MIDGAP_PUMP wraps
the call in `while (SDL_DOSAudioPump()) { }` per seam -- top up the
ring to full per seam. That requires this signature change:
SDL_DOSAudioPump void -> bool.

CONTRACT for the bool return:
- true  = the iterate did meaningful work AND the ring is not yet
          full. The caller MAY call again to top up further.
- false = either the iterate was a no-op (TryLock+timeout backstop
          tripped per SDL/0068; device->shutdown observed; NULL
          device), or the defense-in-depth iter cap fired, or the
          ring is now full (audio thread drains naturally;
          further pumps waste CPU). The caller's `while`-loop exits.

Implementation in SDL_DOSAudioPump (vendor/SDL/src/audio/dos/
SDL_dosaudio_sb.c):
- NULL device -> reset counter, return false.
- Cap check: if calls_since_false_return >= 32, log diagnostic, reset
  counter, return false. (Defense-in-depth against caller-side
  `while`-loop bugs -- lost return check, off-by-one. 32 chunks ~=
  750 ms audio, ~ 2x typical 16-chunk ring depth; cannot false-
  trigger in normal play since a 16-chunk fill needs ~16 iterates.)
- Acquire outer device->lock via SDL_LockMutex (blocking; the
  SDL/0068 amendment wraps this with a TryLock+timeout backstop).
- Run SDL_PlaybackAudioThreadIterate (recursive lock; we hold the
  outer).
- Read ring-room snapshot INSIDE the outer lock for consistency with
  WaitDevice's own room check (DOSSOUNDBLASTER_WaitDevice line 720-
  721 of this file): `(ring_size - (ring_write - isr_ring_read)) >=
  chunk_size`. Same predicate boundary = same definition of "room".
- Release outer lock.
- If has_room: increment counter, return true.
- Else: reset counter, return false.

Counter semantic: "consecutive true-returns within this call-
sequence." Resets on every false-return path so the next call-
sequence (next load_stage seam) starts fresh.

THE THREE SAFETY PROPERTIES STILL HOLD. The v2 while-loop pattern
repeats the Iterate path N times serially; each individual iteration
honors all three properties; the loop introduces no new touch points.
The function-head comment and the file-head comment in
SDL3/SDL_dosaudio_pump.h are updated to document the bool contract +
cap + while-loop pattern explicitly.

Doc-polish landed in this amendment (team-lead approved post-iter):
dropped the "predates nxengine-evo/0162" / "phased-rollout" framing
that became inaccurate when 0067+0162 ship in the same combined iter;
adopted the "6 load_stage seams" specificity + the "A/B-confirm the
Leg A pump against the pre-0162 freeze on real DX2-66 hardware"
rationale for the killswitch.

Two TUs touched: src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c (function-body
rewrite + the cap counter static + the updated function-head comment)
and include/SDL3/SDL_dosaudio_pump.h (signature `void` -> `bool`
on the prototype + the file-head "Engine-side gate" doc-polish +
the function-declaration doc-comment updated for the bool contract).

Rides the re-gated combined DX2-66 iter alongside SDL/0068 v2
(TryLock+timeout backstop, signature ripple) and nxengine-evo/0162-v2
(while-loop caller pattern). build-qa re-gates #84.

Workspace-local per memory/sdl_ai_policy.md; never upstreamed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>
